    "description": "CarbonCount Holdings 1 is a sustainable infrastructure investment vehicle that provides capital to clean energy and climate-positive projects in the United States. Its end markets include developers and owners of renewable, efficiency, and other sustainable infrastructure assets that require long-duration capital solutions. The operating model is capital-intensive but portfolio based, deploying equity and leverage into infrastructure investments rather than running a single operating asset platform. Public disclosures state that the HASI-KKR partnership had closed nearly $3 billion of investment commitments across multiple sustainable infrastructure asset classes through November 2025 and had increased total investment capacity to nearly $5 billion. HASI and KKR formed CCH1 in 2024 and announced an additional $1 billion of capital commitments in December 2025.",
